  "cases": [
    "permits RBAC-only global readers and writers, including inactive organizations",
    "does not let a real legacy flag bypass a disabled platform role",
    "RLS denies forged app.role and commercial reading inherited from a local membership",
    "enforces organizations:read independently after permission revocation on the same token",
    "enforces organizations:read independently after grant revocation on the same token",
    "enforces organizations:manage independently after permission revocation on the same token",
    "enforces organizations:manage independently after grant revocation on the same token",
    "revokes pure RBAC bindings while preserving the explicit legacy flag compatibility",
    "does not grant DELETE or identity-column updates even to an authorized administrator",
    "keeps commercial authority separate from local data and account activity",
    "requires current authority and a real platform organization for both audit proofs",
    "preserves response fields and uniqueness without publishing database errors",
    "revalidates current authority after a real organization lock (revoke)",
    "revalidates current authority after a real organization lock (expire)",
    "rolls back POST and audit when authority expires while audit waits",
    "rolls back PATCH and audit when authority expires while audit waits",
    "audit rejection rolls back mutations without exposing private database details",
    "discards already-read commercial rows if authorization is revoked before the DTO",
    "migration reapplication preserves revocations, other policies, helpers and runtime roles"
  ],
